        "id": 1934715
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-01-29T21:17:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not sure that this accomplishes what you intend to do. I imagine the vendor hook is meant to set `set_fh` to true. But in that scenario, you\u0027ll end up satisfying the set_fh check on line 2018 and return immediately instead of installing the fault handler.\n\nIf it\u0027s false, we\u0027ll also return because of the cookie check.\n\nIt feels like what you want is something more like:\n\n`if (!set_fh \u0026\u0026 domain-\u003ecookie_type \u003d\u003d IOMMU_COOKIE_NONE) { ...`\n\nCorrect?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2016,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 2019,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "6b9b94b279c108966397f9594e0a25c8fc94fc15",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
